The Companion appearance-proposal wiring for the composition root.

`main.ts` is owned by several concurrent branches at once, so this branch ships its wiring here
rather than editing the file, exactly as `companion-memory-main.patch` and
`companion-question-main.patch` did before it.

Applies to web/packages/app/src/main.ts at 27da4d5c513ff81a642828aff037090b83b98415.

    git apply docs/patches/companion-proposals-main.patch

Without it, `mountCompanion` still compiles and still runs. `proposeAppearance` is optional and
absent means every utterance goes straight to `ask`, which is the behaviour the product had
before this path existed. Absent is deliberately NOT the same as a function that answers
"question" for everything: a registered no-op would make "this build cannot propose" and "this
sentence was a question" the same observation, and neither the person nor a record could tell
them apart.

What it costs when it IS applied is one extraction call per utterance, including the ones that
turn out to be questions. That is real and it is stated rather than hidden: the classifier is
what decides what a sentence was, the browser cannot decide it, and the alternative is showing
the style vocabulary to every question about a photograph.

Verified applied on this branch: web typecheck, dependency-cruiser and vitest all pass with it.

